# ${name}

${description}

Built with [Gesso](https://github.com/quoxiom/gesso).

## Getting started

Gesso is not published on PyPI yet, so install it from a checkout first:

```bash
pip install -e /path/to/gesso
```

Then install this project:

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Run it

```bash
${app_id}
```

## What is already wired

- **Application identity** — `src/${package}/app.py` declares the name, id and
  version once, and every path derives from it (`gesso.core`)
- **Typed configuration** — `src/${package}/config.py` declares each setting's
  type, default and constraints; Gesso handles the file format, so people can
  keep JSON, TOML or YAML (`gesso.config`)
- **Internationalisation** — `src/${package}/locales/en.json`, with the user's
  overrides read from their own config directory (`gesso.i18n`)
- **Theming** — `src/${package}/themes/default.json`, a *partial* palette:
  only the tokens worth changing are listed, and the rest come from the
  contract (`gesso.ui.theme`)
- **A window** — `run_app` and a navigation shell, so there is somewhere to put
  your pages (`gesso.ui.app`)

